<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-229 P3.4 (nexus-p2m1x.22; linda's ruling, 2026-11-22): nexus.rdr229_gate_latch, one row per completion-check gate that has held on
    this install. The completion check writes the row for gate 3 the first time it holds (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING) and every
    engine reads it, so a gate that has held stays held: a live gate 3 that goes false later (an id index REINDEXed or rebuilt, so INVALID
    for a while) does not send readers back to the name path, whose indexes retire once gate 3 has latched.

    Columns:
      gate           the primary key: the gate's name ('gate3').
      latched_at     when the check first saw the gate hold.
      engine_version the engine release that wrote it.
      pci_off        true when the gate latched while per-collection indexing was off (NX_SEARCH_PCI=0): no per-collection index was required
                     then, so an engine that later runs with PCI on builds the id indexes first, as if gate 2 held, because readers are on the
                     id either way. false (the default) when the id indexes were required.

    Global table, no tenant column and no row-level security (the posture of data_moves, service_tokens and install_pings): it describes
    the install and holds no tenant data, so it is not in the tenant export registry (that covers the RLS tables) and a tenant export or
    import never reads or writes it. nexus_svc reads and writes it through grants-nexus-svc-1 (the runAlways loop and ALTER DEFAULT
    PRIVILEGES, as for every other nexus_admin-owned table); the check itself writes it on the admin connection. A row from before a database
    restore is not carried by the restore of an older backup: a restored install reads "not latched" and latches again once gate 3 holds.

    Rollback is written verbatim. DDL only, no row DML.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-080-1" author="nexus-p2m1x.22">
        <comment>Create nexus.rdr229_gate_latch, the install-wide latch of the RDR-229 completion check's gates (P3.4). DATA EFFECT: none; one empty table, no row of any other table is read or written.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE TABLE nexus.rdr229_gate_latch (
    gate            TEXT        PRIMARY KEY,
    latched_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    engine_version  TEXT        NOT NULL,
    pci_off         BOOLEAN     NOT NULL DEFAULT false
);
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            DROP TABLE IF EXISTS nexus.rdr229_gate_latch;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
